    },
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p47-q1-3-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Solving $\\cos 2x=\\sin x$ has the same solutions as $$2\\sin^2x+\\sin x-1=0.$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "True.",
          "worked": "Use $\\cos 2x=1-2\\sin^2x$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}1-2\\sin^2x&=\\sin x\\\\2\\sin^2x+\\sin x-1&=0\\end{align*}$$\n\nThese reversible rearrangements preserve all solutions.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 0
      },
      {
        "id": "p47-q1-3-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Solving $\\sin 2x=\\sin x$ has the same solutions as $$2\\cos x=1.$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "False. Cancelling $\\sin x$ loses the solutions for which $\\sin x=0$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}2\\sin x\\cos x&=\\sin x\\\\2\\sin x\\cos x-\\sin x&=0\\\\\\sin x(2\\cos x-1)&=0\\end{align*}$$\n\nEither $\\sin x=0$ or $2\\cos x=1$. The second equation alone omits the first case.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 0
      },
      {
        "id": "p47-q1-3-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "Solving $\\tan 2x=\\cot x$ has the same solutions as $$\\tan^2x=\\frac13.$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "False. The original equation also has solutions with $\\cos x=0$, where $\\tan x$ is undefined.",
          "worked": "For example, at $x=90^\\circ$,\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\tan(2\\times90^\\circ)&=\\tan180^\\circ\\\\\\tan(2\\times90^\\circ)&=0\\\\\\cot90^\\circ&=0\\end{align*}$$\n\nThus $90^\\circ$ satisfies the original equation, but $\\tan^2 90^\\circ$ is undefined. Using the tangent double-angle formula in terms of $\\tan x$ omits the case $\\cos x=0$, so the equations do not have the same solutions.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 0
      }
    ]
  },
